    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Subsection 8B(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022a00048#sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022a00048.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022a00048.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the Human\nRights Commissioner unless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appropriate qualifications, knowledge or\nexperience; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Human Rights Commissioner\nunder a previous appointment under subsection (1).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 48, 2022\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the Human\nRights Commissioner unless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appropriate qualifications, knowledge or\nexperience; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Human Rights Commissioner\nunder a previous appointment under subsection (1).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 48, 2022\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-6-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-6-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022a00048#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Subsection 8B(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the Human\nRights Commissioner unless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appropriate qualifications, knowledge or\nexperience; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Human Rights Commissioner\nunder a previous appointment under subsection (1).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 48, 2022\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(2) Subsection 8B(2)",
