    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Subsection 46B(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022a00048#sch-1-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022a00048.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022a00048.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Social Justice Commissioner\nunless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has significant experience in community life of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Aboriginal and Torres Strait\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022\nNo. 48, 2022\n\nIslander Social Justice Commissioner under a previous\nappointment under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Social Justice Commissioner\nunless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has significant experience in community life of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Aboriginal and Torres Strait\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022\nNo. 48, 2022\n\nIslander Social Justice Commissioner under a previous\nappointment under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022a00048-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022a00048#sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Subsection 46B(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) A person must not be appointed under subsection (1) as the\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Social Justice Commissioner\nunless the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has significant experience in community life of\nAboriginal persons or Torres Strait Islanders; and\n\n(b) the selection of the person for the appointment is the result of\na process that:\n\n(i) was merit-based; and\n\n(ii) included public advertising of the position.\n\n(3) Paragraph (2)(b) does not apply in relation to the reappointment of\na person who, immediately before the start of the period of\nreappointment, holds office as the Aboriginal and Torres Strait\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Legislation Amendment\n(Selection and Appointment) Act 2022\nNo. 48, 2022\n\nIslander Social Justice Commissioner under a previous\nappointment under subsection (1)."
    },
